        "title": "Such reverred deity deserves better upkeep of premises",
        "text": "Pashupatinath is a revered deity and a very important temple which every devotee of Lord Shiva seeks or aspires to visit and worship. This temple admits only Hindus and has large parking areas on all sides. After walking through sprawling walk ways, one enters the main gate where celestial bull, Nandi's backside is seen prominently from outside.\nOnce inside, there are serpentine queues after which one enters crowded and lowly lit passages around the main hall which is even smaller. \nPlace around has dozens of smaller temples but all around monkeys scare you. So do crowds jostling, burning offerings to lamps. \n\nAll in all, one feels such an important temple must be kept cleaner and flow of visitors directed if not controlled better.",
