        "title": "Depends on your time of visit",
        "text": "Being an Indian,I had heard a lot about this place,and this was the first place I visited when I was in Kathmandu.Went there around 4 PM,what hit me was the melancholy with the burning bodies and mourning families.Photography is prohibited,and the main shrine was closed.apparently they only open it once a fortnight.The crowd depends on what time to visit,and also the days of the week\nMake sure you visit the adjoining hilly area where you can enjoy some nature sans the smell of death.",
